<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE-SAfrica budget borrowing requirement/finance.</title>
<headline>TABLE-SAfrica budget borrowing requirement/finance.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following table contains the South African government's borrowing requirement and financing plans for 1997/98 as presented by Finance Minister Trevor Manuel in his budget speech on Wednesday:</p>
<p>    (rand bln)			1997/98	   1996/97</p>
<p>    Estimated expenditure	 186.747	   176.070</p>
<p>    Estimated revenue	     161.976	   145.808</p>
<p>    Projected deficit		24.771	    30.262</p>
<p>    Less: Opening balance	     000	     6.738</p>
<p>    Net borrowing requirement    24.771	    23.524</p>
<p>Loan redemptions:</p>
<p>    * Short-term (net)		  000		 000</p>
<p>    * Government stock/bonds     10.828	    16.697</p>
<p>    * Premium on govt stock	 - 200	    -1.100</p>
<p>    * Foreign loans			69	     1.554</p>
<p>    * IMF loan			  1.381		 345</p>
<p>    Gross borrowing requirement  36.849	    41.020</p>
<p>Financing:</p>
<p>    * Short-term (net)		2.000	     2.000</p>
<p>    * Government stock	     27.702	    34.241</p>
<p>    * Foreign loans		   4.000	     2.831</p>
<p>    * From IMF deposit at SARB    1.381		 345</p>
<p>    * From strategic fuel fund    1.250	     1.603</p>
<p>    * From sale of state assets     516		 000</p>
<p>    Total financing		  36.849	    41.020</p>
<p>-- Parliamentary newsroom +27 21 403-2502</p>
